
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:foreach@

%9Parameters:%9

    SERVER:     Runs the command once for every connected server, with that
                server active.
    CHANNEL:    Runs the command once for every joined channel, on all
                servers, with that channel as the active item.
    QUERY:      Runs the command once for every open query, on all servers,
                with that query as the active item.
    WINDOW:     Runs the command once in every window, with that window,
                its active item and its server active.

    The command to run; the command character is added when it is missing.

%9Description:%9

    Repeats a command for each server, channel, query or window. The command
    is run as if it had been typed in that context, so commands that act on
    the active server, channel or window act on each one in turn.

    After FOREACH WINDOW, the window that was active before becomes active
    again.

%9Examples:%9

    /FOREACH SERVER /NICK alice
    /FOREACH CHANNEL /SAY I will be back in a few minutes
    /FOREACH QUERY /SAY Sorry, I have to go now
    /FOREACH WINDOW /CLEAR
    /FOREACH WINDOW /WINDOW LEVEL -JOINS -PARTS -QUITS

%9See also:%9 CHANNEL, QUERY, SERVER, WINDOW

